---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Publish" description="Expose a port on your tharavad VM.">
  <h1>Publish</h1>

  <p>
    Optional. If you want the public internet to hit a process on your VM,
    declare it in git.
  </p>

  <pre>{`# user-vms/you.nix
publish = [
  { port = 3000; }                     # → http://you.tharavad.xyz
  # { subdomain = "blog"; port = 8080; }  # → http://blog.tharavad.xyz
];`}</pre>

  <p>
    After rebuild, the front door routes that hostname to your guest port. You
    still have to run something that listens:
  </p>

  <pre>{`python3 -m http.server 3000 --bind 0.0.0.0`}</pre>

  <p>
    No process on the port means a proxy error, not a broken DNS entry. SSH and
    HTTP share the same names on different ports: twenty-two for shell, eighty
    for the web path.
  </p>

  <p>
    This is not a PaaS with auto deploys. It is a pipe you control. Keep it
    small, or make it weird. Both are allowed. Publish is HTTP too, same
    statement as the brochure: if you need TLS for your app, terminate it
    yourself in the guest or wait until we grow up and run ACME for real
    reasons, not vibes.
  </p>
</Base>
